UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 267(d), the related party buyer may reduce (but not below zero) any gain recognized on a subsequent sale to an unrelated party by the amount of the seller''s previously disallowed loss. The daughter can use the $15,000 disallowed loss only to offset gain, not to create or increase a loss.
Wrong (A): The disallowed loss cannot create a loss on a subsequent sale. It can only reduce recognized gain, and any unused portion is permanently lost.
Wrong (C): The buyer''s basis remains at the purchase price ($45,000). The disallowed loss does not adjust basis; it is a separate offset against future gain.
Wrong (D): The disallowed loss benefit applies only to gain on the specific property sold, not to unrelated income from other sources.$EXPL$
