  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Rolling (or dynamic) conformity means a state automatically incorporates federal IRC changes as they are enacted without requiring separate state legislation. Centerville''s reference to the IRC "as currently in effect" is the hallmark of rolling conformity.
Wrong (B): Freezing conformity to a specific date describes static (or fixed-date) conformity, which is the opposite of rolling conformity.
Wrong (C): Requiring separate legislation each year to adopt federal changes describes selective or annual conformity, not rolling conformity.
